# Org-to-bucket mapping for `discover-orgs.sh --from-csv`.
#
# Maintain this file (or any CSV in the same shape) when you already know
# which orgs your IAM principal can reach and don't want to probe Athena —
# faster, no AWS calls, no IAM read perms needed.
#
# Copy to a real path (gitignored: .agents/orgs.csv) and edit:
#   cp .agents/orgs.csv.example .agents/orgs.csv
#   $EDITOR .agents/orgs.csv
#   bash .agents/tools/discover-orgs.sh --from-csv .agents/orgs.csv > .env.suggested
#
# Format: comma-separated, header row optional, lines starting with `#` ignored.
#   Columns: org_id, bucket, name (3rd column is informational, not emitted).
#
# Region is auto-detected from each bucket via `aws s3api get-bucket-location`;
# don't add a region column — it's not needed.

org_id,bucket,name
00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001,root-data-adapter-production,Example Production Org
00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002,root-data-adapter-clientname,Example Client-Specific Org
